    <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.65); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 16px; padding: 36px 32px; box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);">
      <span style="background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.12); color: #c084fc; border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">LEGAL COMPLIANCE</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory RTO Paperwork, Transit Marine Insurance &amp; Delivery Handover for Bike Transportation Electronic City</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When arranging bike transportation to or from Electronic City, the logistics team must assemble a concise set of documents that satisfy both local regulatory bodies and the carrier’s compliance requirements. The first requirement is a self‑attested photocopy of the vehicle’s Registration Certificate (RC).</p>
<p>The photocopy should be signed by the owner or the authorized transporter, and a stamp or digital signature confirming its authenticity must be affixed. This document proves the bike’s legal status and ownership, preventing any title‑related disputes during transit.</p>

<p>The second key document is the current Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate. The certificate must be issued within the last 30 days of the departure date, and it must show a “Good” rating.</p>
<p>The PUC is mandatory for any vehicle crossing state borders and ensures that the bike complies with environmental norms. A copy of the PUC, together with the RC photocopy, should be scanned and stored in the carrier’s digital filing system.</p>

<p>Insurance coverage is the third pillar of the paperwork bundle. A valid insurance certificate, issued by a recognized insurer, must cover the bike’s full declared value. In the case of marine transit, the carrier prefers a 100 % declared‑value marine transit insurance policy.</p>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">This policy protects the bike against loss, theft, or damage that may occur while it is on board a vessel or in a storage facility.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The insurance certificate should include the policy number, coverage limits, and the exact value declared for the bike.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The carrier’s risk management team will cross‑verify the policy against the vehicle’s market value before approving the consignment.</span></li></ul>

<p>Finally, the IBA‑approved consignment bilty is mandatory for all freight movements in the region. The bilty, issued by the Indian Bureau of Aeronautics (IBA) or a recognized freight forwarder, serves as a receipt of goods and a contract of carriage.</p>
<p>It must list the bike’s description, weight, dimensions, consignor and consignee details, and the agreed freight rate. The bilty should be signed by both parties and retained in the shipment’s electronic logbook.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


